# OpsCore Control Plane secrets -- install as /etc/opscore/controlplane.env
# (mode 0600, owner opscore). This file is the ONLY channel for these two
# values: they are never written on the unit's command line (argv is visible
# to every local user) and never into the JSON deployment config.
#
# Prefix note (ADR-091): OPSCORE_<KEY> is the canonical spelling across the
# product; the historical OPESCORE_<KEY> spelling (one letter transposed)
# remains accepted as a compatibility alias, and the canonical name wins when
# both are set. Env values take precedence over KEY=VALUE config files.
#
# OPSCORE_JWT_SECRET signs access and refresh tokens (HS256). Use at least 32
# random bytes, hex or base64 (no spaces or quotes). Rotating it invalidates
# all previously issued tokens.
OPSCORE_JWT_SECRET=

# OPSCORE_ADMIN_PASS bootstraps the admin user on first run of a persistent
# (sqlite) deployment. Phase 27 policy applies: at least 12 characters, not a
# known default, and not equal to the username.
OPSCORE_ADMIN_PASS=
